            "created_at": "2025-08-08T15:18:07.761469+00:00",
            "notes": "The 8/7/2025 buffed the scalar to barrier health gained proportional to money earned to 150%, up from 100%. I'm honestly really surprised that they did this because his barriers are already pretty sustainable. Regardless, we want to take advantage of this as soon as possible by getting [Philharmonic Fortitude](item_e31e2686-cb66-4f89-9779-88a0cbc16e07). This will increase your survivability drastically thanks to the increased uptime of your Experimental Barrier alongside the buffs to his barrier health scalar.  [Trinisphere](item_ffaf0527-137c-4fa6-8048-82f2c99f6d56) is still a usable first power depending on the matchup, but [Philharmonic Fortitude](item_e31e2686-cb66-4f89-9779-88a0cbc16e07) is certainly more consistently successful when getting it Round 1. While  [Trinisphere](item_ffaf0527-137c-4fa6-8048-82f2c99f6d56) is an easy way to boost your damage right off the back, [Philharmonic Fortitude](item_e31e2686-cb66-4f89-9779-88a0cbc16e07) increasing survivability is more valuable in most situations. You do more damage when you're alive than when you're dead, after all!\n\nDepending on the matchup, [First Aid Kit](item_0172eaaa-1902-44a3-b989-d12f0f7301da) might be a nice choice if you can keep your distance. [Field Rations](item_46ae6709-1166-426f-bca3-97a538d3f089) is also a potential option if it's a good map for it.\n\nYour main goal this round is to earn as much money as possible. If the enemy is playing grouped up often, spam your primary fire into them to get a lot of splash damage off. Cycle your abilities accordingly to prevent your Experimental Barrier breaking (though this should be relatively easy with [Philharmonic Fortitude](item_e31e2686-cb66-4f89-9779-88a0cbc16e07).",
