            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-08-08T15:18:07.761469+00:00",
            "notes": "Here's where your carry potential spikes. Picking up [Orbital Barrier](item_208bfd6a-6b32-46d8-b815-458b0d072c29) and [De Kuiper's Thesis](item_d2ca1240-ec35-48c0-bc19-f6376af032b4) together gives you good self-sustainability, as the item also applies to [Orbital Barrier](item_208bfd6a-6b32-46d8-b815-458b0d072c29) alongside your Experimental Barrier. Coupled that with [Philharmonic Fortitude](item_e31e2686-cb66-4f89-9779-88a0cbc16e07) and those barriers become really tough to take down! \n\nTry to snag both [Talon Modification Module](item_c0ca1795-a3ea-4dc9-ae17-f34122574b3a) and [Velocity Vector](item_5ad7884b-ac8c-42f4-a5ad-359f43270540) if you haven't already and fill the rest of your item slots with Common items. Don't stress if you can't afford them, though; as long as you have [De Kuiper's Thesis](item_d2ca1240-ec35-48c0-bc19-f6376af032b4) and a mixture of WP and attack speed, you'll be good to go.\n\nIf you're struggling a bit from taking a lot of damage, considering grabbing [Crusader Hydraulics](item_b64cee07-ca32-405d-987e-868b415bbc09) here to help with that.\n\nYou want to keep both of your barriers up as much as possible, so cycle your abilities strategically to maintain those strong sources of healing. Also, remember that your barriers heal your team too! Staying grouped together can really be beneficial in keeping your team up. Your healing will also help you get your Ultimate faster and farm more money!",
